tool_args.new_string:
\paragraph{Post-SFT accuracy does not predict GRPO outcome.}
\label{sec:sft_gradient}
Under SFT alone, CKA-only (63.91\%) $>$ \rasp{} (61.49\%) $>$ Standard (59.29\%), yet under GRPO the \rasp{}/Standard ordering reverses (peak 0.081 vs 0.061).
More strikingly, ShortGPT post-SFT (44.73\%) shows GRPO actively harming accuracy ($-$1.36\,pp), while unstructured pruning achieves the highest post-SFT accuracy (87.87\%) but zero GRPO improvement ($\Delta{\approx}$0\,pp).
Post-SFT accuracy does not monotonically determine GRPO recovery outcome; the recovery capacity gradient is driven by structural properties of the pruned architecture, not residual SFT quality.

